{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant","id":1417993,"title":"3e Deathlords... could actually be pleasant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-13T00:04:33-07:00","id":1417993,"title":"3e Deathlords... could actually be pleasant?","content":"So just something that came to mind while I was discussing the subject on the Exalted Discord. Could the Deathlords be... not complete and utter douchebag-bosses this edition?<br /> <br /> I mean:<br /> <br /> 1. The relationship between Abyssal and Deathlord is supposed to be closer in 3e, and not necessarily antagonistic.<br /> 2. Previous edition &quot;bad examples&quot; have been given a makeover to keep their essence but bring them more in line with what players want in a mentor (see Raksi)<br /> 3. Previous edition &quot;fake religions&quot; like the Immaculate Philosophy have been rendered in 3e &quot;true, for a certain value of true&quot;, could Oblivion not fall under the same heading?<br /> <br /> Take one example, the Bishop of the Chalcedony Thurible, this guy:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/thirdexalt/images/a/a0/The_Bishop.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/243?cb=20141011060243\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> He's super evil right? Pushing a false Oblivion focused shining path, his true form is a poison leaking void beast, he's getting the girl in the picture to slice her throat e.t.c....<br /> <br /> But what does he want actually? Like REALLY wants?<br /> <br /> In the fullness of time, he wants all beings to, fully of their own free will, reject the suffering of the cycle of reincarnation and embrace the peace of Oblivion and non-existence.<br /> <br /> Like, I could see this guy being one of the most <b>HEROIC </b>(or saintly, if you prefer) of Deathlords in fact.<br /> <br /> War orphans, people suffering from incurable disease, widows and the poor, he could be out there doing his 101% best to make sure they make it so that they don't die without having had a chance to fully contemplate the Shining Path he offers. Oblivion doesn't necessarily have to be a fake creed, it could have the same treatment as the Immaculate Philosophy in this edition.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the devs are thinking in that direction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 10-13-2020, 06:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T00:58:02-07:00","id":1417997,"title":"","content":"I think there's definitely scope to present the nihilism of death in a balanced light. But mostly, the Realm is evil but your Dragon-Blooded doesn't have to be. Same deal for Dearthlords and Abyssals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T02:51:18-07:00","id":1418005,"title":"","content":"In My Creation i've reskinned the Lover as a particularly dark take on the Fairy Godmother trope who mastered the metaphysics of the underworld (and necromancy) and has a deep understanding of the passion plays of the dead. When she takes an interest in someone (positive or negative) it is always deep, almost obsessive and <i>very </i>personal, so if she likes you she will break every boundary she needs to to get you what you desired and ask for nothin in return, and then just smile when you suffer the distaste of having what you once wanted. For her deathknights this means she'll make <i>certain</i> you get what you wanted from the life you left behind (love, revenge, fame, whatever) and will ask you to help her on whatever her latest obsession is (did you piss her off, then she will make absolutely sure to meticulously <i>destroy </i>everything you cared about until you beg for oblivion).<br /> <br /> I also remade Eye as a Liv Octavius style character who was always the Star of Dirt and Doubt with the mummy just being a puppet she uses to keep her rule from distracting her from her work, now she mostly eaves the administrative tasks to her abyssal polycule while she furthers her experiments. For her deathknights this means being a lot more hands-off but also being given a lot more power and authority than most deathlords grant and expects her abyssals to be much more supportive of both each other and her latest projects, whatever they may be (ever wonder what happens to water dragons immersed in lethe, let's find out together!).<br /> <br /> May or may not change these up after 3e Abyssals but this is how I'm running it for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","user":"Darkfoxdev","date":". 10-13-2020, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T03:06:34-07:00","id":1418006,"title":"","content":"Like for sure there are some/lots of *<b>EVIL, EVIL, EVIL</b>* Deathlords (I submit that you can still make the Mask of Winters play that role).<br /> <br /> But I wonder if maybe Oblivion doesn't have to be<i> inherently</i> evil this edition, just the antithesis of <b><i>Creation </i></b>(which would definitely be enough reason to fight against it if you were so inclined).<br /> <br /> I mean, the 3e core already has Death Knights focusing on the Romance of the Grave, so maybe thats the direction we're headed towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 10-13-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T03:26:50-07:00","id":1418008,"title":"","content":"I believe 3e Silver prince is going this direction, being focused on the idea of Transcendence through death and building a good society for both the living and the dead in his realm. It was mentioned on the Discord that the basic quality of life in his realm was better than most even for the living, it has a clear direction of upward momentum and his point that being a ghost is superior to being a regular un-exalted mortal isn't exactly <i>false </i>considering the power (and ability to increase essence) that ghosts can acquire and mortals cannot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T08:52:06-07:00","id":1418054,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why the Deathlord couldn't put in a creed talking about how oblivion and staying in the Underworld can be a good idea. Creation is a shitty, shitty place, especially for mortals, and for mortals, they can actually get a power-up by dying. Which says a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T02:12:56-07:00","id":1418162,"title":"","content":"I'm all for some of the Deathlords being charming and pleasant to engage with when they're well-disposed to you, and even one or two that have a certain endearing roguish quality towards opponents that haven't pissed them off too much. But my preference is for them to all ultimately have a villainous quality in setting and narrative, for various meanings of the word, and for none of them to exactly have a good reason for doing what they're doing even if it's not malicious for all of them.<br /> <br /> Take the Bishop; the idea of all souls being liberated by being carried into the darkness by him is all well and good, but I would lean towards it originating in a lot of ego and bitterness, even if kept deeply buried, that has little concern for alternative viewpoints.<br /> <br /> I'd also prefer for considerations of oblivion for any of them to be kept to a minimum, and that being compelling is more often about arguments for the merits of the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T03:57:46-07:00","id":1418168,"title":"","content":"Each Deathlord has deliberately chosen to embrace the Neverborn and aligned themselves against creation. That doesn't mean they can't have noble goals, ending the suffering of souls in perpetual agony (as they see it) of reincarnation could be seen as noble from that viewpoint. I'm not sure they'd ever get into a place I would call &quot;Right&quot; or &quot;Heroic&quot; but there is definitely some room in there. That has been the case since the ending parts of second edition, where the Return of the Scarlet Empress book had a section on how in a creation ruled over by Yozis the release of oblivion might actually be kinder and proposed that as a seed for an abyssal campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9124-satoshi","name":"satoshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T05:51:55-07:00","id":1418181,"title":"","content":"I feel like there should be room for a &quot;Party Deathlord&quot; who embraces a hedonistic, for-tomorrow-we-shall-die philosophy of the end of all things. Like, he's perfectly happy to let those currently living run out the clock and see the world off with a bang, because this is the <i>final</i> generation.<br /> <br /> Just need to find a non-squicky way to convey a deathlord whose approach to breaking the cycle of life and death is preventing new life rather than prematurely bringing on death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T07:46:59-07:00","id":1418188,"title":"","content":"The Bishop is by far the readiest candidate for an \u201cActually pretty chill\u201d treatment. Literally all it takes for the Shining Path to not (necessarily) be an evil fake religion brainwashing people into tragic supersuicide is for the books to not call it one in those exact words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418181#post1418181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just need to find a non-squicky way to convey a deathlord whose approach to breaking the cycle of life and death is preventing new life rather than prematurely bringing on death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Define \u201cnon-squicky.\u201d Where does passing around overdoses of maiden tea fall? Or they could just be very strictly only drugs and rock &amp; roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 10-14-2020, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T11:13:11-07:00","id":1418219,"title":"","content":"The best way to do that is to massively increase the tech level and prosperity, then put out free amounts of birth control drugs. And lots of servitors. <br /> <br /> Look at modern day countries and at how the birth rate is dropping, requiring immigration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T12:15:14-07:00","id":1418225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418168#post1418168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Deathlord has deliberately chosen to embrace the Neverborn</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of want embracing the Neverborn to amount to nothing more than a necessity for squeezing the Powerthirst out of them.<br /> <br /> They desperately need an interesting Death to lord it over, as an alternative to all this non-existance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T13:06:17-07:00","id":1418239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418225#post1418225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of want embracing the Neverborn to amount to nothing more than a necessity for squeezing the Powerthirst out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what it is? There's only so much the Neverborn can do about it if you decide the Underworld is pretty cool and you don't feel like feeding it to Oblivion any time soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:24:42-07:00","id":1418375,"title":"","content":"I'd personally portray the Abyss as the deepest parts of the underworld, revealed by the deaths of the Neverborn. Not Oblivion, because I feel that term lacks nuance, but a primeval, infinite darkness in which impossible things and dead realities churn and come together into a sort of anti-life. Very much a &quot;Sacred Darkness&quot;, if not one that is wholly good(or wholly evil).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:50:28-07:00","id":1418380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418239#post1418239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's exactly what it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am responding to a statement that reads to me as giving it more than that.<br /> <br /> I ask sincerely; did you read my repeat of the term &quot;embrace&quot; as also suggesting some element of pledging themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:59:08-07:00","id":1418386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>satoshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418168#post1418168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Deathlord has deliberately chosen to embrace the Neverborn and aligned themselves against creation. That doesn't mean they can't have noble goals, ending the suffering of souls in perpetual agony (as they see it) of reincarnation could be seen as noble from that viewpoint. I'm not sure they'd ever get into a place I would call &quot;Right&quot; or &quot;Heroic&quot; but there is definitely some room in there. That has been the case since the ending parts of second edition, where the Return of the Scarlet Empress book had a section on how in a creation ruled over by Yozis the release of oblivion might actually be kinder and proposed that as a seed for an abyssal campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that the vast majority of Deathlords, while they may have signed up to murder the world....aren't actually interested in doing that. They've learned that they have to at least toe the line after they saw what happened to the First and Forsaken Lion, but even Deathlords like the Lover who are actually sincere in their commitment to serving what they understand the will of the Neverborn to be mostly don't want to destroy Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:04:46-07:00","id":1418393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418386#post1418386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the vast majority of Deathlords, while they may have signed up to murder the world....aren't actually interested in doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, this just feels like unnecessary extra steps to me.<br /> <br /> Was there not a conception of moving away from presenting the Neverborn as something that you can make agreements with or possessed of a will?<br /> <br /> And we're sticking with the idea that the First and Forsaken Lion was deliberately punished for an infraction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:24:53-07:00","id":1418396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418386#post1418386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that the vast majority of Deathlords, while they may have signed up to murder the world....aren't actually interested in doing that. They've learned that they have to at least toe the line after they saw what happened to the First and Forsaken Lion, but even Deathlords like the Lover who are actually sincere in their commitment to serving what they understand the will of the Neverborn to be mostly don't want to destroy Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that the Neverborn are.......<i>conflicted</i> about destroying Creation? Insofar as they are capable of having opinions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:46:56-07:00","id":1418397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418393#post1418393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there not a conception of moving away from presenting the Neverborn as something that you can make agreements with or possessed of a will?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords swore pacts to serve the will of the Neverborn. The Neverborn are not in a state of lucidity or coherence that would facilitate actually communicating that will to the Deathlords, but the Deathlords include a number of genius savants and occultists, so they've been able to put together some conjecture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And we're sticking with the idea that the First and Forsaken Lion was deliberately punished for an infraction? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Deliberately&quot; is questionable, given the state of the Neverborn, but the Deathlords understand the First and Forsaken Lion's fate to have been a punishment for just completely ignoring Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:47:48-07:00","id":1418398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1417993-3e-deathlords-could-actually-be-pleasant?p=1418396#post1418396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does this mean that the Neverborn are.......<i>conflicted</i> about destroying Creation? Insofar as they are capable of having opinions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deathlords range from &quot;conflicted&quot; to &quot;actively disinterested in destroying Creation.&quot; As far as the Deathlords and Abyssals can tell, they don't think the Neverborn are conflicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}